translation:
Wind fierce, the sky high, gibbons cry in grief;
The islet clear, sand white, birds wheel and turn.
Leaves fall beyond all bounds, a rustling rain;
The river rolls, ceaseless, forever on.
Ten thousand miles, autumn's grief, a guest for life;
A hundred years of illness, alone I climb.
Hardship and bitter hate have frosted my hair;
Wrecked, I have just set down my cup of wine.

