translation:
The Nation Broken

The nation is shattered, yet mountains and rivers remain;
Spring returns to the city, where grass and trees grow deep.
Grieved by the times, flowers splash my eyes with tears;
Hating parting, birds startle my heart.
War beacons have blazed for three months on end;
A letter from home would be worth ten thousand pieces of gold.
I scratch my white hair until it grows thinner still,
Barely able now to hold a hairpin.

