{"translation": "Leaning on the railing of the high tower, feeling the gentle breeze;
Gazing far, the sorrow of spring rises darkly from the horizon.
In the fading sunset, amid grass and misty light,
Silent, no one understands my intent as I lean against the rail.

I meant to act wildly, seeking drunkenness alone,
To sing with wine in hand—yet forced joy tastes bland.
Though my clothes grow loose and wide, I will never regret it;
For her sake, I willingly endure this wasting away."}

